# Bounded wider FP16 probe after v28 validation

This runbook does not execute the probe. Root retains exclusive GPU control.
The unchanged original ordinary kernels are tested; no timings or full FP16
network claim are produced. Stop at the first parity, integrity or sanitizer
failure and preserve its report.

## Activation files

Copy these reviewed drafts without changing their bytes:

| Source | Active destination | Needed for runtime |
|---|---|---|
| `tools/vendor_fp16_window_proof.py.draft` | `tools/vendor_fp16_window_proof.py` | Yes |
| `tools/vendor_fp16_window_probe.py.draft` | `tools/vendor_fp16_window_probe.py` | Yes |
| `tests/test_vendor_fp16_window_cpu.py.draft` | `tests/test_vendor_fp16_window_cpu.py` | CPU tests |
| `tests/test_vendor_fp16_window_probe_cpu.py.draft` | `tests/test_vendor_fp16_window_probe_cpu.py` | CPU tests |

Keep the draft siblings during this activation. The reviewed helper explicitly
prefers the proof's `.py.draft` sibling, falling back to `.py` when absent;
either must have the exact pinned hash. The two staged test modules currently
load their `.py.draft` helper/proof explicitly. No C++/CUDA file or compilation
dependency is introduced, and no package entry point changes are needed.

Expected SHA256 values:

- Proof: `9e19ca4c78cea80d56ddc99295d301b7f004fa74aca93c3aef84f1f856e2d9ff`.
- Probe: `e8aed5b17e93d737f0aa5c0bc2e161856dafbd4f3a95642562102ff93e36e61d`.

Existing imports were checked: `tools.vendor_fp16_inventory` supplies pinned
entry parsing and fragment maps; `tools.extract_assets` supplies the pinned
DLL/resource and record extraction; `tools.vendor_benchmark` supplies the
guard allocator and original driver module wrapper; `tuning.policy` supplies
JSON writing. CPU conversion also uses `dlssnr.geometry.fused_layout` and
`dlssnr.weights.tiled_token`. Only the `execute` function initializes CUDA or
loads an original cubin. It imports the existing `InferenceBlock` and
`InferenceNumerics` and leaves their FP16 arithmetic unchanged.

The assets are the original DLL/resource, `module_1/2/3.ptx` and matching
`module_1/2/3.cubin`. Their hashes and exact ordinary entry bodies are pinned
inside the helper/proof. The independent CPU tests also need `assets/nr`.
No dependency on the C32 FP16 probe is introduced.

## Exact first memcheck command

Run from `D:\Research\DLSSNR-PyTorch`, only after installing and validating
v28. The discovered sanitizer entry point is CUDA 13.4's Windows batch wrapper.
The command below selects 8x8 inputs, all four phases, all four fixtures and
ordinary encoder blocks 5, 9 and 15. It runs 48 cases, 144 ordinary replays
and 144 poisoned graph replays. The helper first reruns the exact requested
CPU address proof before any native module or tensor allocation.

```powershell
& "C:\Program Files\NVIDIA GPU Computing Toolkit\CUDA\v13.4\bin\compute-sanitizer.bat" --tool memcheck --launch-timeout 300 --error-exitcode 99 --target-processes all --log-file outputs\vendor_fp16_window_v28_memcheck.log .\.venv\Scripts\python.exe tools\vendor_fp16_window_probe.py --execute --blocks 5 9 15 --height 8 --width 8 --phases 0 1 2 3 --fixtures identity_residual ffn_basis attention_basis real --device 0 --seed 721 --output outputs\vendor_fp16_window_v28.json *> outputs\vendor_fp16_window_v28.log
if ($LASTEXITCODE -ne 0) { throw "Wider FP16 probe or memcheck failed; retain both logs and JSON." }
```

Require `completed=true`, `executed_gpu=true`, `all_byte_exact=true`, exactly
48 `exact=true` cases, three ordinary and three poisoned graph replay records
per case, and a zero-error sanitizer summary with no other nonzero/error
summary. The report records the actual installed extension hash; verify it
matches the intended v28 binary. Every native allocation guard and immutable
input/weight is checked, as are all externally supplied candidate operands.
The candidate result is allocated by the extension and retained/byte-checked;
it does not have a separate external red zone.

The helper saves mismatch byte counts and output hashes instead of accepting
approximate equality. `native_speed`, `dll_host_executed`, and
`dll_host_conversion_verified` must remain false. A passing result is bounded
ordinary-entry parity using derived Half checkpoint records.

## Follow-up only after the first result passes

Run a separate output path for the decoder blocks and a partial shifted-window
shape; this adds different real weights and boundary CTAs:

```powershell
& "C:\Program Files\NVIDIA GPU Computing Toolkit\CUDA\v13.4\bin\compute-sanitizer.bat" --tool memcheck --launch-timeout 300 --error-exitcode 99 --target-processes all --log-file outputs\vendor_fp16_window_v28_decoder_memcheck.log .\.venv\Scripts\python.exe tools\vendor_fp16_window_probe.py --execute --blocks 63 57 49 --height 12 --width 20 --phases 0 1 2 3 --fixtures identity_residual ffn_basis attention_basis real --device 0 --seed 721 --output outputs\vendor_fp16_window_v28_decoder.json *> outputs\vendor_fp16_window_v28_decoder.log
if ($LASTEXITCODE -ne 0) { throw "Decoder FP16 probe or memcheck failed; retain both logs and JSON." }
```

After memory safety and numerical parity pass, a bounded shared-memory
racecheck can use the first command with `--tool racecheck`, distinct log/JSON
paths, and `--fixtures real`. Do not infer racecheck success from memcheck or
from the CPU shared-epoch proof.
